No ancient author quotes or paraphrases this poem (no literary testimonium is known); it survives solely on the two papyri listed above, both 20th-century finds, so there is no witness earlier than 1914 and the poem is absent from pre-papyrological collections (confirmed absent from Wharton's 1885 'Sappho: Memoir, Text, Selected Renderings' and not separately numbered in Edmonds' 1922 Loeb 'Lyra Graeca', which predate or do not incorporate the join with P.Oxy. 2166(a), 1941/1951).

